@ 14.2 - Proto-Elamo-Dravidian to Achaemanid Elamite
# citation: Pogostick Man, from McAlpin, David W. (1974), “Toward Proto-Elamo-Dravidian”. Language 50(1):89 – 101
	{i,e,u} > ∅ / :{ #_ta, #_na }:
	e > e, i / #C_C
	w > ú / V_ (Mc:[+affricate]lpin uses the accented-vowel notation due to some apparent height-contrast neutralizations before /a/)
	k > ∅ / V_V
	ŋk > k / V_V
	ŋk:[+long] > k:[+long] / V_V
	mp > p, p:[+long] / V_V
	c > s / :{ #_a, #_u }:
	ɲc > ns / V_V
	r̀ > r / :{ V_V, V_C }:
	ŕ > r:[+long] / V_V
	nr̀ > nr
	l > n / V_#
	v > m / #_V (?)